/**
 * The top bar dropdowns and small product scenes of the homepage, rebuilt 1:1
 * from the desktop app's components (pzza-code 0.2.94): the Port manager
 * (src/panels/PortsMenu.tsx), Notifications (src/panels/Notifications.tsx and
 * the approval answers of src/ui/PermissionPrompt.tsx), Quick Chat
 * (src/panels/QuickChat.tsx), the command palette
 * (src/panels/CommandPalette.tsx), Agent usage (src/panels/UsageMenu.tsx and
 * UsageSpend.tsx) and the workspace tabs (src/grid/WorkspaceTabs.tsx). The
 * markup, class names, icons and tooltip texts are the app's, styled by the
 * app's own stylesheet (app.css). Each dropdown panel is exported on its own,
 * anchored against the window's right edge like the app's Dropdown, so the
 * interaction layer can open it from any window scene.
 *
 * While its scene is on screen, each panel plays the feature it shows, the
 * way the app does it (helpers in panel-loops.tsx, playback in playback.ts):
 * a port is forwarded, an approval is answered and the agent's result comes
 * in, Quick Chat answers a question, the palette filters as a query is typed,
 * the usage limits refresh and the workspace tabs switch. Any press or
 * keystroke in a scene stops its loop and leaves the visitor in charge.
 */
